	"web_text": "Reverse appliqué: a variation of appliqué, in which patterns are cut into the top layer of cloth, exposing the underlying fabrics.The appliqué technique is used throughout many cultures. In the main gallery you will find appliqué work in the Kuba Woman's Ceremonial Skirt from the Republic of Congo, the Egungun dance costume from Yoruba people of Nigeria, the Ceremonial robe from the Ainu, the indigenous peoples of Japan, and in the late nineteenth century day dress from French designer, Jeanne Paquin.",
